      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2017 The Authors. Published by WILEY-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim.",
        "AbstractText": "Masked by rotational anisotropies, xthe nonlinear chiroptical response of a metamaterial is initially completely inaccessible. Upon rotating the sample the chiral information emerges. These results highlight the need for a general method to extract the true chiral contributions to the nonlinear optical signal, which would be hugely valuable in the present context of increasingly complex chiral meta/nanomaterials."
      },
